Falsifies `pci::verification::a_fresh_bus_queue_holds_the_root_and_nothing_else`.

The defect: the root bus is queued but not marked seen, dropping `q.seen[0] = 1`. This is the
base case the induction above it needs, and the harness's own doc comment predicts exactly this
error: someone adjusting `from_the_root` without reading the harness next to it. A walk still
works on every well-formed topology, because a bridge naming bus 0 is a firmware bug, so
nothing short of the proof notices.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(q.tail == queued && q.tail == 1)`, where `queued` is
zero and `tail` is one: the invariant the `enqueue` proof preserves is false in the initial
state, so preserving it proves nothing.

